294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (The growing availability of advanced weapons, intelligence, and private military companies has made proxy wars more sophisticated and extremely difficult to regulate. States can provide financial, logistical, and military support to proxy actors while maintaining distance from the conflicts themselves. Allowing them to pursue their strategic interests, including access to valuable resources and greater regional influence, without directly implicating themselves in conflict.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E ( The UN has expressed concern over the current reality of proxy wars around the world; however, despite sanctions and peacekeeping efforts, enforcement remains inconsistent, and many external actors continue to provide varying forms of support to parties involved in conflict. The involvement of multiple states and non-state actors makes it difficult to determine responsibility and hold sponsors accountable. )
/Pg 16 0 R
